__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){"use strict";Object.defineProperty(e,'__esModule',{value:!0}),Object.defineProperty(e,"PRIVACY_MARKDOWN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return n}}),Object.defineProperty(e,"TERMS_MARKDOWN",{enumerable:!0,get:function(){return o}});const n="# Privacy Policy \u2014 The Mechanic\n\n**Last updated:** 16 September 2026\n**App:** The Mechanic, a free fan-made Elder Scrolls Online fight-guides app (trials, dungeons, arenas).\n**Owner:** Ivan Rodriguez.\n\nThis is a plain-language privacy policy for a small fan app. It is not legal theater. The Mechanic is **not affiliated with** Bethesda Softworks, Zenimax Online Studios, ZeniMax Media, or The Elder Scrolls\xae Online.\n\n**This app is not for children under 13.** We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child under 13 created an account, contact the owner so the account can be deleted.\n\n## Who this is for\n\nPlayers 13 or older. Fight guides work **offline on this device** with no account. Optional cloud sign-in (email and password, Google, or Apple) is available if you want a cloud account.\n\n## What we collect\n\n- **Nothing required to use Mechanics.** Notes, favorites, theme, and accent color stay on this device unless you sign in.\n- **Account / email (optional)** \u2014 Sign-in (email/password, Google, or Apple). Email lives in the auth system and is copied onto your profile. Apple may give a relay address (privaterelay.appleid.com) if you hide your email.\n- **Profile (optional)** \u2014 Username, display name, platform, avatar if you upload one, accent color.\n- **Push tokens** \u2014 Only if you opt in on a phone build. Deleted on sign-out. Web does not register a push token.\n\nWe do **not** collect precise location, contacts, health, payment cards, or government IDs.\n\n## Analytics\n\n**None.** The Mechanic does not embed Google Analytics, Facebook SDK, advertising SDKs, or similar trackers. We do not sell your data. We do not use it to advertise to you.\n\nCrash or usage metrics that Expo or the store might collect on a future standalone build are those vendors\u2019 policies, not extra analytics we added in this app.\n\n## Who sees what\n\nAccess is enforced by the server (row-level security), not only by the app UI, for any optional cloud account.\n\n- **You** can read your own profile.\n- Guild, roster, DM, application, and character-sheet cloud rows from The Armory product may still exist on the shared backend. This standalone app does not expose those features in the UI.\n\n## Third parties that process data for us\n\n- **Supabase** (hosted Postgres + Auth) \u2014 Optional accounts and database.\n- **Expo** \u2014 App runtime, and Expo\u2019s push API when a phone token is registered.\n- **Google Sign-In / Apple** \u2014 Optional identity providers.\n\n## How long we keep it\n\nUntil you delete your account, or the owner deletes the project. Signing out leaves the cloud account in place. **Delete my account** (Settings) removes the auth user and cascades related public data.\n\nDevice-only extras (theme, accent, mechanics favorites) live on that device\u2019s storage.\n\n## Your choices\n\n- **Export my data** \u2014 Settings. Downloads JSON of what this signed-in client can read.\n- **Delete my account** \u2014 Settings. Confirm, then we call a server function as **you** (never a secret key in the app) and sign you out.\n- **Skip accounts entirely** \u2014 Use Mechanics without signing in.\n\n## Contact\n\n**Ivan Rodriguez**, owner of The Mechanic. Use Settings \u2192 About in the app, or the GitHub repository for this project. There is no separate support inbox in this build.\n\nIf you are in a region with a statutory privacy request (access, delete, correct), use Export / Delete in Settings first, then contact the owner if something is still missing.\n\n## Fan disclaimer\n\nThe Elder Scrolls\xae Online and related marks belong to ZeniMax Media and its affiliates. The Mechanic is an unofficial fan companion. Skill tooltips and icons credit ESO-Hub where shown in-app.\n",o="# Terms of Use \u2014 The Mechanic\n\n**Last updated:** 16 September 2026\n**App:** The Mechanic.\n**Owner:** Ivan Rodriguez.\n\nThese terms are short on purpose. By using the app (with or without an account), you agree to them.\n\n## 1. What this is\n\nThe Mechanic is a **free, unofficial** companion for Elder Scrolls Online fight guides: trials, dungeons, and arenas. It is meant to work **offline-first**. Cloud sign-in is optional.\n\nIt is **not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by** Bethesda Softworks, Zenimax Online Studios, ZeniMax Media, or The Elder Scrolls\xae Online. Game names and lore belong to their owners. Skill tooltips and icons may credit ESO-Hub.\n\nThe owner may change, pause, or shut down the app (including any hosted database) without a paid SLA.\n\nThe Armory guild companion is a **separate product** (the `main` branch / Armory Pages demo). This app is not that product.\n\n## 2. Age\n\nYou must be **13 or older**. The app is not directed at children under 13. We ask you to confirm that on first use and at optional sign-up (email, Google, or Apple).\n\n## 3. Your account\n\n- Sign-in is **optional**. Mechanics does not require it.\n- If you sign in: **email and password**, **Google**, or **Apple**. Phone / SMS is not offered.\n- Keep your password to yourself. The owner cannot read it.\n- One human per account; no bulk signup, scraping, or bots.\n\n## 4. Acceptable use\n\nDo not:\n\n- Harass, threaten, or share others\u2019 real-life private data.\n- Spam, phish for accounts, or upload malware.\n- Pretend to be Bethesda, the owner, or another player.\n\n## 5. Content and IP\n\nFan use of ESO names in fight notes does not make this an official product. Do not upload content you do not have the right to share.\n\n## 6. No warranty\n\nThe app is provided **as is**. Guides can be incomplete or out of date. Cloud sync can lag, fail, or be limited by the free hosting plan.\n\n## 7. Privacy and deletion\n\nThe Privacy Policy explains what we store. You can export or delete an optional cloud account in Settings.\n\n## 8. Changes\n\nIf these terms change in a material way, we will bump the date here. Continued use after that date is acceptance. The in-app copy is the same document.\n\n## 9. Contact\n\n**Ivan Rodriguez**, owner. Settings \u2192 About, or the project\u2019s GitHub page.\n"},702,[]);
